    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "I think that taking away the secretary's authority on the CCC again that's kind of insider baseball for a lot of people but when you look at the range of things that Secretary Vilsack has been able to use that for whether it was the supply chain problems getting us through the pandemic or the fertilizer shortage trade issues. There's something for every state that happens in there and it's one of the few ways you can really deal with some of the huge problems that we face in agriculture when you have a Congress that has a hard time acting.",
